@startuml
!include theme.iuml
title One desktop save attempt, including failure boundaries
start
:Enter expression, annotations,\nlanguage and optional audio;
:Review current evidence;\napprove only if justified;
:Press Save / Ctrl+Enter;
if (Recording, stop or audio save unfinished?) then (yes)
  :Explain retry/finish or deliberate discard;\nkeep draft; do not append;
  stop
else (no)
endif
if (Trimmed expression nonempty?) then (no)
  :Show Missing text;\nkeep draft for correction;
  stop
else (yes)
endif
:Generate ID and timestamp;\naccept approval only for exact reviewed values;
:Locked read-modify-write;\nwrite/fsync sibling and atomically replace CSV;
if (Commit succeeded?) then (no)
  :Report storage failure;\nretain draft and staged audio;
  stop
else (yes)
endif
:Release committed audio from draft ownership;\nreset form, retaining contributor;
:Clean remaining draft-owned resources;\nreport any cleanup error for retry;
:Load one snapshot for count,\nrecent entries, Browse and Stats;
if (Refresh succeeded?) then (yes)
  :Display refreshed views and Saved status;
else (no)
  :Preserve views; report read error;\ncommit remains successful;
endif
stop
legend bottom
  Preserved desktop compatibility only; web saves use private WorkspaceStore transactions.
  Diamonds represent exclusive guarded decisions, not parallel work.
  One final node ends this attempt, not the collector application.
  Duplicate warnings are advisory on desktop; API duplicates return 409.
  File staging is separate; recording details appear in the sequence view.
endlegend
@enduml
